## What Gets Stripped vs. What Stays

### ❌ REMOVED from stock L4T Ubuntu
| Component | Why removed |
|-----------|-------------|
| systemd | Replaced by `onyx-init` — 100x lighter, boots in <1s |
| NetworkManager | Replaced by minimal `wpa_supplicant` + `dhcpcd` |
| snapd, cloud-init | Bloat — not needed on embedded |
| X11 / Wayland / GNOME | No display server — HUD is direct framebuffer or SSH TUI |
| apt / dpkg | Agents are the new "packages" — hot-loaded, not installed |
| journald / rsyslog | Replaced by structured event stream |
| cron, at | OnyxD handles all scheduling |
| man pages, locales, docs | Space savings (~200MB) |
| Unused kernel modules | Custom `.config` strips unused drivers |

### ✅ KEPT (essential for AI inference)
| Component | Why kept |
|-----------|---------|
| Linux kernel 5.15 (L4T) | NVIDIA GPU driver compatibility |
| NVIDIA kernel modules | GPU compute (CUDA, cuDNN, TensorRT) |
| cgroups v2 | Resource isolation per agent |
| `/proc`, `/sys`, `/dev` | Hardware monitoring (thermal, power) |
| BusyBox | Minimal shell + core utils for debugging |
| `wpa_supplicant` | WiFi connectivity |
| `openssh-server` | Remote access for development |
| `libcuda`, `libnvrtc` | CUDA runtime for inference |

### Target Rootfs Size
| Image | Size |
|-------|------|
| Stock L4T Ubuntu | ~12 GB |
| **OnyxOS rootfs** | **~800 MB** (kernel + CUDA + agents) |

