### Phase 3: onyx_sched.ko — Kernel Scheduler Module

#### [NEW] `onyx-sched/` — Kernel module

```
onyx-sched/
├── Makefile
├── onyx_sched.c          # Main kernel module
├── onyx_sched.h          # Shared structs with userspace
└── onyx_sched_ioctl.h    # ioctl interface for OnyxD
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The Jetson kernel is 5.15 — no `sched_ext` support (requires 6.12+).
> Instead, we implement a **userspace-assisted scheduler** via:
> 1. A kernel module that exposes agent priority/cgroup controls via `ioctl`
> 2. OnyxD in userspace runs the Lagrangian auction and pushes decisions to the module
> 3. The module enforces CPU affinity, nice values, and cgroup bandwidth throttling

**How it works:**
```
OnyxD (userspace)                    onyx_sched.ko (kernel)
    │                                      │
    │  1. Run Lagrangian auction            │
    │  2. Compute: ADMIT/SUSPEND/EVICT     │
    │                                      │
    ├──── ioctl(ONYX_SET_AGENT_STATE) ────→│
    │     { agent_pid, state, cpu_shares,  │
    │       mem_limit, nice_value }        │
    │                                      │
    │                              3. Set cgroup params
    │                              4. Adjust nice value
    │                              5. Set CPU affinity
    │                              6. Apply mem.max
    │                                      │
    │←──── ioctl(ONYX_GET_METRICS) ────────│
    │     { cpu_usage, mem_usage,          │
    │       context_switches, thermals }   │
```

**Key ioctl commands:**
- `ONYX_REGISTER_AGENT` — Register a new agent PID with the scheduler
- `ONYX_SET_AGENT_STATE` — Update agent state (running/suspended/evicted)
- `ONYX_SET_RESOURCE_LIMITS` — Set cgroup limits (CPU shares, mem.max, GPU partition)
- `ONYX_GET_METRICS` — Read per-agent resource consumption
- `ONYX_GET_THERMALS` — Read all thermal zones in one syscall
- `ONYX_EMERGENCY_THROTTLE` — Immediate power reduction

