### Phase 4: OnyxD — The Central Daemon (Rust + Cython)

#### [NEW] `onyxd/` — The brain of OnyxOS

```
onyxd/
├── Cargo.toml                    # Rust workspace member
├── src/
│   ├── main.rs                   # Daemon entry point
│   ├── config.rs                 # Parse /etc/onyx/system.toml
│   ├── thermal.rs                # Thermal governor (reads sysfs)
│   ├── power.rs                  # Power monitor (INA3221)
│   ├── cgroup.rs                 # cgroup v2 controller
│   └── ipc.rs                    # Unix socket IPC for agents
├── market/                       # The market scheduler (Cython)
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── auction.pyx               # Lagrangian auction engine
│   ├── quant_ladder.pyx          # Quantization ladder
│   └── agent_itd.py              # Agent ITD (unchanged from v1)
├── inference/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── engine.py                 # llama-cpp-python wrapper (dev)
│   └── engine_rs.pyi             # Type stubs for Rust engine (prod)
└── hud/
    ├── __init__.py
    └── dashboard.py              # Rich/Textual TUI (from v1)
```

**OnyxD lifecycle:**
1. Parse `/etc/onyx/system.toml` — load hardware config + agent manifests
2. Open `/dev/onyx_sched` — connect to kernel module
3. Start thermal monitor thread — poll thermal zones at 10Hz
4. Start power monitor thread — poll INA3221 at 5Hz
5. Load inference engine — initialize llama.cpp with CUDA
6. Start agent registry — scan `/etc/onyx/agents/` for manifests
7. Start market ticker — run Lagrangian auction at 1Hz
8. Start IPC server — listen on `/run/onyx/onyxd.sock` for agent connections
9. Start HUD server — expose dashboard on localhost:8080 or terminal

