### Phase 5: Agent System

#### [NEW] Agent manifest format (`/etc/onyx/agents/*.toml`)

```toml
# /etc/onyx/agents/emotion.toml
[agent]
name = "emotion_rt"
class = "RT_HARD"
description = "Real-time emotion detection from camera"
binary = "/opt/onyx/agents/emotion_agent"
model = "/opt/onyx/models/emotion-v1.gguf"

[resources]
base_utility = 100
power_watts = 5.0
ram_mb = 1024
gpu_tops = 8.0
is_rigid = true

[quantization]
levels = ["FP16", "INT8"]  # Only these levels supported
utility_exponent = 0.5

[inputs]
camera = true
microphone = false

[outputs]
emotion_label = "string"
confidence = "float"
```

#### [NEW] `agents/` — Built-in agents

```
agents/
├── base_agent.py             # Abstract base with IPC to OnyxD
├── emotion_agent.py          # RT_HARD — camera → emotion
├── voice_agent.py            # RT_SOFT — mic → NLU → LLM → TTS
├── world_model_agent.py      # RT_SOFT — camera → spatial map
└── loop_agent.py             # BG — background reasoning
```

Each agent:
1. Connects to OnyxD via Unix socket (`/run/onyx/onyxd.sock`)
2. Registers itself with its manifest
3. Receives `ADMIT`/`SUSPEND`/`EVICT` signals from OnyxD
4. Requests inference from the shared engine (or runs its own)
5. Reports metrics back to OnyxD

